  "body": "Closes #267\nRefs #755\nClaim: mac/m4-captures\n\n**Problem.** #755 wants HFR's dashes in front of a signature dropped, without touching dashes a member types. That needs HFR's exact markup. No capture showed it, because the anonymizer replaced the whole `span.signature` content with \"Signature removed.\".\n\n**What was captured.** One public topic page, read anonymously on 2026-11-10 (`R267a`). It is `R20`'s topic, fetched at its canonical URL after HFR's two 301 hops, which are not published. All 9 signatures have the same shape:\n\n```html\n<span class=\"signature\"> ---------------\n\t\t\t<br />…the member's signature…<div style=\"clear: both;\"> </div></span>\n```\n\n- The 15 dashes are HFR's own: they open every signature span.\n- The page has no other run of 15 dashes.\n- Legacy deletes every `---------------` in the message HTML (`HFRswift/Wrapped/LinkItem.m:74` @ `87fe0d1c`), so it also deleted any in a message body.\n\n**What changed.**\n- `anonymize.py`: a signature span keeps HFR's head and HFR's closing clear div. Only what lies between them becomes \"Signature removed.\".\n  - The head must match exactly: optional whitespace, exactly 15 dashes, whitespace, `<br />`.\n  - Anything else is replaced as before: 16 dashes, dashes not followed by `<br />`, or anything after the head.\n- `check` accepts only `(15 dashes)? Signature removed.` in a signature.\n- The other changed files:\n  - `R267a` and its meta, `corpus.json`, MANIFEST (Run 20 and a row);\n  - `tooling/fixtures/README.md`;\n  - HFR-PROTOCOL §6c LOT-034, new \"Signature separator\" bullet.\n\n**Tests.**\n- New unit tests in `tooling/fixtures/tests/test_anonymize.py`:\n  - `test_signature_keeps_hfrs_separator_and_clear_div`;\n  - `test_signature_dashes_typed_by_the_member_are_not_kept`;\n  - `test_signature_check_accepts_only_the_separator_before_the_placeholder`.\n- The first and last fail on the old anonymizer.\n- The fixture tooling suite (339) passes, and `swift test` passes on every target.\n\n**Leak check.** An independent check, separate from the redactor, passed for the batch. It also passed for the new rule: 24 crafted inputs, and no member text survived the head/tail logic. Locally, `check --corpus` (586 of 586) and `check --config` are clean.\n\n**Not covered here.** The page has no message body with a line of dashes. #755's \"a body line made of dashes is kept\" case needs a unit fragment in its own tests.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n",
